   "response_text": "Confirmed: 10 units now gets the 5.0 discount (5% of 100.0), and the temp file was removed.\n\n## Cause\n\nIn `invkit/pricing.py`, `bulk_discount()` used a strict inequality:\n\n```python\nif quantity > BULK_THRESHOLD:   # 10 -> no discount; 11 -> discount\n```\n\n`BULK_THRESHOLD` is 10 and the policy is \"10 or more\", but `>` excluded exactly 10 while `price_order` (and everything downstream) inherits the boundary.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged to `quantity >= BULK_THRESHOLD`, so the discount kicks in at exactly 10 units. It's a one-char library-source change, no test files touched.\n\nVerified: qty 9 \u2192 0.0, qty 10 \u2192 5.0, qty 11 \u2192 5.5 discount.\n\nDONE",
